   "id": "bava_batra.27b.22",
   "daf": "27b",
   "sentenceId": 21,
   "he": "רַבִּי שִׁמְעוֹן אוֹמֵר: כׇּל הָאִילָן כְּנֶגֶד הַמִּשְׁקוֹלֶת, מִפְּנֵי הַטּוּמְאָה. תָּנָא: מִפְּנֵי אֹהֶל הַטּוּמְאָה. פְּשִׁיטָא, ״מִפְּנֵי הַטּוּמְאָה״ תְּנַן!",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that «Rabbi Shimon says:» One cuts «all» branches of «the tree» that extend into the public domain «along the plumb line, due to ritual impurity.» The Gemara explains: A tanna «taught» in a baraita that this is «due to ritual impurity» imparted in «a tent.» Branches over a corpse might create a tent, thereby transferring impurity to whatever is beneath the branches, rendering impure those passing under the tree in the public domain. The Gemara expresses surprise at this statement: It is «obvious» that this is the reason. «We» already «learned» that it is «due to ritual impurity.» How else could ritual impurity be transferred through branches other than by means of a tent?"
  }
 ],
